#{[{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125390} :activity/id #uuid "6257a384-69ce-502a-8a3f-5b199a93b00a" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125390 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125780 :tutorial/content "Suppose we are given an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ invertible matrix $A.$ Remember that if $A$ is invertible, then the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the trivial solution $\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\nLet's extract all possible information from this fact using the vector spaces related to the matrix, namely, the *column space* and the *null space*.\n\n- The fact that the unique solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ is $\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ tells us that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Null}(A)=\\{ \\mathbf{0} \\},\n$$\n\n or alternatively, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A)) = \\textrm{nullity}(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Furthermore, if $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=0$ then $A$ has no *non-pivot* columns, or equivalently, all the columns of $A$ are *pivot columns*. So \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Col}(A))=\\textrm{rank}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n- Finally, since $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ is a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^n$ and its basis has $n$ linearly independent vectors, we can conclude that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^n.\n$$\n\nAll the results mentioned above can be summarized in the following theorem, called the **invertible matrix theorem**:\n\n*Let $A$ be an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n![](images/7e/7ef5d72a30dd7f79f6182c4d78d705a7771f9f90ff0bb50f6d539614cb1e5b4d.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "555ca00c-d37e-5c67-a658-69b087390920" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3522 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "4620379b-2eed-5dd7-bf3a-9edf0b4aea79" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125592}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125391 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799"} :step/id #uuid "77230797-e80e-5644-8b1e-9e3722a0b66d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125591}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125591 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc"} :step/id #uuid "7ebf299f-89ad-55ae-8fe6-d0af3bc56dfd"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125592 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124630 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "879514d5-e127-5485-ab41-d459f6b5f379"} :step/id #uuid "debf1d2f-c0e6-5c61-b195-a95710e2c35e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125391}}] :activity/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Dimension, Rank and Nullity" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124685} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435679} :activity/id #uuid "26e5acff-8db9-5e5d-9122-36baf139baac" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435677 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435676 :question/id #uuid "ea4581af-a083-51da-803f-0f83b3ed2ea6"} :step/id #uuid "42d8e8b3-7048-5f94-884b-ae373fb59042" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435678}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435678 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272239 :question/id #uuid "8dad0d98-37c5-5af9-9c0a-4f0fabec2bcc"} :step/id #uuid "9a467517-2fb7-54c3-b455-e47e7392ef56"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435679 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124863 :question/id #uuid "a5b63a26-4713-5ecd-9d64-befaccc0bd77"} :step/id #uuid "d2193342-5bc1-5a6f-99d1-42bf1fad6047" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435677}}] :activity/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Dimension, Rank and Nullity" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435669} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485604} :activity/id #uuid "7e6f49d0-b97d-5a05-9f9c-64559727441e" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485601 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426072 :question/id #uuid "251cfe7e-474d-59b2-8ccf-101401daf068"} :step/id #uuid "1140fa5b-f47a-5b21-a507-87491673347d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485610}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485604 :step/content {:db/id #