n from ${R}^{7}$ into ${R}^{7},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{7} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=7 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nSince $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\nT({v}_{1})=T({v}_{2})\\,⟹\\,T({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since ${v}_{1}-{v}_{2}\\in \\text{Ker}(T)$ and ${v}_{1}\\ne {v}_{2},$ we must have that $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0},$ the transformation $T$ and the matrix $T$ are not invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $T$ is not invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272287 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6e6c5d7-e923-5b79-aeca-92ce53c73074" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449640} {:answer/id #uuid "709274c3-c137-53e6-a5e6-794fdfe9a85a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449641} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d40a1ee-aefc-57fa-8071-7deb8e4a3305" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7181c58-f5c1-540e-9c79-9a178187acc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449642} {:answer/id #uuid "451e520e-366e-5d15-a3ef-e0067131fc93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449642} :answer-field/id #uuid "53ef3a30-34f3-5c51-826c-d16c38c6f3d2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450775} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8801d71e-6668-5c1b-93c6-53060eac64bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449644} {:answer/id #uuid "e2ff3c94-ccfa-5b45-b2dc-3dd9301a301e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449645} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e1e1146-8542-54b0-b796-f3070052fa06" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450776}] :question/id #uuid "c894da3b-5f0a-59a9-8060-52795d04ecee" :question/math-academy-id "q-141460" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $T:{R}^{7}\\to {R}^{7}$ is a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T,$ and $T(x)=v$ has no solution for some vector $v?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $T$ is not invertible\n- **II.** $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$\n- **III.** $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 7$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{7}$ into ${R}^{7},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{7} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=7 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $T(x)=v$ has no solution, we have that $v\\notin \\text{Im}(T),$ hence $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{7}.$ According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{7},$ the transformation $T$ and the matrix $T$ are not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $T$ is not invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $T$ is not invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272288 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2f591c8-5dc6-5a9b-9834-d348ea0ba55c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449646} {:answer/id #uuid "d971d1ca-d302-5135-9b9b-8a59d4eedb5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449647} :answer-field/id #uuid "901e996e-5f74-5811-9119-b09127f872b7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450777} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fa48495-2a69-53c0-a6eb-907afb28c8eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449648} {:answer/id #uuid "0fd370f2-c3e7-59ac-9b60-dbdab11ac477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449649} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f7b6165-7688-5b31-b8de-bb5f0df45e64" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e5738f6-983e-551f-b134-397efd15e8e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449650} {:answer/id #uuid "444ee7a0-efba-54ea-bdd4-105d434eca39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {