\\end{bmatrix}$ does not lie in $\\text{Im}(T)$, then $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{2}.$ Therefore, according to the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{2}$, then $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 2.$\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{2},$ the transformation $T$ can't be invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afa82d44-d03d-5e9b-af04-272ab90230e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464096} {:answer/id #uuid "71f897c8-dfce-5b45-8f4c-bb7062ae467e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464096} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ed222a1-7190-5964-99bc-a9de5fd0be28" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464982} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a1a3dca-d308-5f38-927f-67b0c977e32e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464098} {:answer/id #uuid "d292b59f-adc1-58d1-98bc-5da647707c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464099} :answer-field/id #uuid "cafebd75-e7fa-54e1-9bcf-2578d3061be4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464983} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbb177f8-879b-5898-9551-53329abe91c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464100} {:answer/id #uuid "7332d203-8792-51a5-976c-10e58a391aaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464101} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8de8dc2-3957-5b43-9b1f-bfdfb462141b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464984}] :question/id #uuid "1cac76f2-abeb-58d4-87e9-5f3619bedd4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-140085" :question/problem "Let $T:{R}^{5}\\to {R}^{5}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n*If $\\text{rank}(T)=5,$ then $\\text{__________}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n- **I.** $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne \\{0\\}$\n- **II.** $T$ is invertible\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{5}$ into ${R}^{5},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=5 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $\\text{rank}(T)=5,$ the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $\\text{rank}(T)=5,$ the invertible matrix theorem implies that $T$ is invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $T$ is invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{nullity}(T)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272291 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8230d7a2-4524-54a5-9590-04c588c295e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464210} {:answer/id #uuid "14884516-4125-50da-8b5d-7e51e9e24ab8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464211} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f5eda39-3b08-5189-b208-4e35abe1db47" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465039} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44af8797-c814-5748-994f-92b788de154a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464212} {:answer/id #uuid "78baedc7-0e87-5ff1-9a52-276bee40b842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464212} :answer-field/id #uuid "d424f77d-314f-5358-8eee-a8487ea9871f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465040} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26f9634b-041a-572d-8750-407c23f61424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464214} {:answer/id #uuid "fa4ff653-5f79-56df-815d-652606c37fae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464214} :answer-field/id #uuid "52b0634f-8af8-5969-84d2-36ca3ab0045a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465041}] :question/id #uuid "496f9381-a057-5d31-a929-726bf731d70b" :question/math-academy-id "q-141495" :question/problem "Let $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T,$ and ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\in {R}^{3}.$  Consider the following statement:\n\n*If $2T({v}_{1})-3T({v}_{2})=0$ and ${v}_{1}\\ne k{v}_{2}$ for all $k\\in R$ then $\\text{__________}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n- **I.** $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne \\{0\\}$\n- **II.** $\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{3}$\n- **III.** $T$ is invertible\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{3}$ into ${R}^{3},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=3 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $2T({v}_{1})-3T({v}_{2})=0$ and $T$ is a linear transformation, we have $T(2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2})=0$ which means $2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2}\\in \\text{Ker}(T).$   Since ${v}_{1}\\ne k{v}_{2}$,  we must have $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne \\{0\\}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the transformation $T$ is not a bijection. Since $T$ is not a bijection, then by the invertible matrix theorem, $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{3}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{3},$ the corresponding matrix $T$ can't be invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272301 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "defa38e6-4b2a-547a-9785-5f2fca155634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464216} {:answer/id #uuid "8813679f-0971-5e77-ad51-40eb57c572d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464216} :answer-field/id #uuid "52c26432-913d-5735-b0ed-85a46e70c8e8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e92260a8-5b4e-5b4e-9416-0de5fe12aa8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464218} {:answer/id #uuid "dadfcb43-c958-54de-8830-025222c2a86f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464219} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ed304dd-c00f-5c24-a7ac-a6a45f1bc15d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465043} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e24f08c0-cbc9-5eb8-b862-7b5254467338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464220} {:answer/id #uuid "2f5185ec-576f-5f3f-890e-3d67f76bcb32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464221} :answer-field/id #uuid "fac72699-e49d-525e-92b7-897f36bc8dae" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465044}] :question/id #uuid "c4507db3-2027-5030-88fd-955381171b17" :question/math-academy-id "q-141569" :question/problem "Let $T:{R}^{4}\\to {R}^{4}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n*If $\\text{nullity}(T)=4,$ then $\\text{__________}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n- **I.** $\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{4}$\n- **II.** $T$ is not invertible\n- **III.** $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 4$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{4}$ into ${R}^{4},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=4 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0,$ the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0,$ the invertible matrix theorem implies that $T$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $T$ is not invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32d41688-d441-5144-8654-a972f8be5b21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464222} {:answer/id #uuid "8e89bfdc-e0ea-5cb6-9225-4a56ce59f56c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464223} :answer-field/id #uuid "72f72fce-9abb-5a6c-9689-b54025b14cfe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465045} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7398f9ee-d9ed-555a-acc0-735e4fdaa78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464224} {:answer/id #uuid "73635a76-1329-52e8-bd4c-7b079d5a02a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464224} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5214e79-29e2-5009-b0e1-02450bcb5417" :answer-field/key "