trix theorem, since $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0},$ the transformation $T$ and the matrix $T$ are not invertible. Since $T$ is not invertible, by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have that $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{6}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{6},$ the invertible matrix theorem implies that the transformation $T$ is not a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364145 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfe45e96-b6f2-5280-bd02-15325098a1c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469032} {:answer/id #uuid "d1208062-b192-5bb7-a768-32fe16db1321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469032} :answer-field/id #uuid "01a567c0-0023-5025-af7d-e7a0249210c8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470128} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e99694d5-15bf-5e3c-9954-8af1c80b4a01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469034} {:answer/id #uuid "427ca074-860f-5ae5-b4a1-3f89a485e8d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469034} :answer-field/id #uuid "338eec5c-2406-5f0c-bb1c-c1531ce433f3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470129} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64b50964-d370-5d75-8291-5c06aa29eca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469036} {:answer/id #uuid "7af62786-7b5e-59ed-ad41-57aa0b2131b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :ans