92186271707}] :question/id #uuid "9859f901-d01e-5f5b-a45d-d37e251b90a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-141449" :question/problem "$T$ is a $$ $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=n \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n$\\,⟺\\,$  $T$ is invertible\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $T:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n}$ is a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* (in terms of linear transformations) states the following: \n\n $T$ is a $\\text{bijection}$ $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=n \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n$\\,⟺\\,$  $T$ is invertible\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is \"bijection\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b6b1031-c163-56a3-b97a-72be4e32e1d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269493} {:answer/id #uuid "6ac4a6d3-74ff-526d-bd44-d7fcf3c957c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270218} {:answer/id #uuid "84b6d79c-90d5-50ff-911d-921429761446" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{n}\\times {R}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270413} {:answer/id #uuid "beb6e7a6-3c2b-58b0-9c1a-4205d23ae0c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R\\times R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270954} {:answer/id #uuid "ef503765-71a5-5455-8a63-fccc8a3da2ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270218} :answer-field/id #uuid "942dfe4b-1180-58a6-b0ed-009c7ca2ed69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271773}] :question/id #uuid "b9558da9-260d-5307-957b-694ef011704b" :question/math-academy-id "q-141447" :question/problem "$T$ is a bijection $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)= \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=n \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n$\\,⟺\\,$  $T$ is invertible\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $T:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n}$ is a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* (in terms of linear transformations) states the following: \n\n $T$ is a bijection $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=n \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n$\\,⟺\\,$  $T$ is invertible\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is ${R}^{n}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272283 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09669a08-0424-55f6-a37b-ad69ae9a1da8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{dim}(\\text{Ker}(T))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269354} {:answer/id #uuid "82eccdab-9956-5f23-a58e-49219d604214" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Domain}(T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270400} {:answer/id #uuid "a9bde013-82da-524f-b418-d676110db9cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270781} {:answer/id #uuid "e2eb01f8-cd4c-5e39-bf38-328dbe974c91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Range}(T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271266} {:answer/id #uuid "f534ced1-f1fa-5110-aebb-6f2d4f6e460f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Ker}(T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Ker}(T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271421} :answer-field/id #uuid "12030f3d-29e4-5e9e-a9a7-adb83737a159" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271536}] :question/id #uuid "74b33e25-b150-5023-89c8-8ae56ab3acbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-141451" :question/problem "$T$ is a bijection $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=n \\\\  & ={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n$\\,⟺\\,$  $T$ is invertible\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $T:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n}$ is a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* (in terms of linear transformations) states the following: \n\n $T$ is a bijection $\\,⟺\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=n \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n$\\,⟺\\,$  $T$ is invertible\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\text{Ker}(T).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272284 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "079f5dae-bfcf-5b50-ba4b-ae83bc6f55b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{Im}(T)$ and $\\text{Ker}(T)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269339} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1d9335-bfdb-5b54-9538-0501d53fbad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{Null}(T)$ and $\\text{Ker}(T)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270657} {:answer/id #uuid "abe72a0c-363a-5a3a-8cac-526a5e9222e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{Ker}(T)$ and $\\text{Domain}(T)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270803} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ee4548-b055-5785-a92c-1b09684993d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{Domain}(T)$ and $\\text{Range}(T)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270889} {:answer/id #uuid "c93ea908